Activation: wait for a spawned service for as long as its process is alive, and report a failed activation with dbus-daemon's own error.

MUST apply after unique-activation.patch (the "z" name sorts it last).

A fixed 25 s wait turned host load into a ServiceUnknown. xdg-desktop-portal
activates its backend before it claims org.freedesktop.portal.Desktop; the
portalshot probe's call (which includes that activation) takes 8.6 s on an
idle host and 18.8 s on a busy one, and on a busier one the 25 s ran out
while the frontend was still starting: "ServiceUnknown: The name
org.freedesktop.portal.Desktop was not provided by any .service files" after
~25 s, with the .service file present (portalshottest.py x86_64: 2 of 10 runs
failed on a host at load average 46, 0 of 8 more on a quiet one). The message
is the generic one because send_msg turned every failed activation into
reply_service_unknown.

Now, as dbus-daemon does:
  * a service whose process is alive is waited for up to 120 s (the session
    bus service_start_timeout); at the cap the caller gets
    org.freedesktop.DBus.Error.TimedOut "Failed to activate service 'N':
    timed out (service_start_timeout=120000ms)";
  * a service that exits non-zero without claiming the name fails at once
    with org.freedesktop.DBus.Error.Spawn.ChildExited "Process NAME exited
    with status N", or Spawn.ChildSignaled "Process NAME received signal S"
    (dbus-spawn-unix.c _dbus_babysitter_set_child_exit_error); exit status
    0 is ignored and the wait goes on, as in bus/activation.c
    pending_activation_finished_cb ("a program may (misguidedly) daemonize");
  * a failed exec replies Spawn.ExecFailed; a second caller waiting on the
    same activation follows the spawner's in-flight marker and fails with it;
  * ServiceUnknown is kept for a name no .service file provides.
Covered by `leandros-sysbus activation-test` (regress: busdact).

